_Sustainability is no longer a side project. Clients, investors and employees now expect businesses to show real progress, backed by real evidence. We spoke with Dr. **Naomi Marden**, Head of Operations, about how SkootEco can help._

### Who is SkootEco?

SkootEco is an ESG consultancy and sustainability platform. We help businesses understand their environmental and social impact, act on it with confidence, and show their progress in a way people can trust.

Our clients range from founder-led companies to large organisations, and they are based all over the world. What they share is a desire to do sustainability properly: measured, verified and built into how the business runs.

We were named one of the [UK's most innovative new businesses](https://skoot.eco/articles/skoot-named-among-uks-most-innovative-new-businesses), an [edie Awards finalist](https://skoot.eco/articles/skooteco-named-finalist-for-consultancy-of-the-year-at-net-zero-awards) in 2024 and 2025, and we are a Top 5% [B Corp](https://www.bcorporation.net/find-a-b-corp/company/skootridecom-ltd/).

### What inspired SkootEco?

SkootEco was founded by CEO Greg Gormley, a serial entrepreneur. A life-changing accident gave Greg a new perspective on what truly matters. He came out of it determined to build a business that creates real value for people and the planet.

That conviction still shapes everything SkootEco does today.

